  <section id="quality-check">
    <h2>How to Perform a River Water Quality Check UK</h2>
    <p>
      If you are standing on the bank asking yourself, "is it safe to swim in the river today?", you are already taking the most important step in wild swimming: risk assessment. River conditions change rapidly due to heavy rainfall, agricultural runoff, and shifting currents.
    </p>
    <p>
      Before you get in, use our live data tool below to verify the current conditions.
    </p>
    <p>
      Understanding the bacterial and chemical safety of a river is vital. A river water quality check uk relies on monitoring sewage discharge alerts and agricultural runoff. In our experience integrating environmental API data, water quality drops significantly within 48 hours of heavy rain.
    </p>
    <p>Look out for these visual warning signs:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Blue-green algae:</strong> Looks like pea soup or green paint on the surface; highly toxic to humans and dogs.</li>
      <li><strong>Milky or murky water:</strong> Often a sign of recent agricultural or sewage discharge.</li>
      <li><strong>Excessive foam:</strong> While some foam is natural, large, foul-smelling accumulations indicate chemical pollution.</li>
    </ul>
